  "title": "sync: don't hold a mutex permit while yielding for coop budget",
  "user": {
   "login": "Jeremiah-D",
   "id": 235112616,
   "type": "User",
   "html_url": "https://github.com/Jeremiah-D"
  },
  "body": "Fixes #8772.\n\nA task driving a FuturesUnordered of futures that lock the same mutex, while locking it itself between polls, deadlocks on 1.54.x once the coop budget runs out: lock() takes the permit and then yields for budget, and the permit ends up stranded on a future that never gets polled again.\n\nTwo changes in batch_semaphore.rs, both restoring the \"a Pending lock() holds no permit\" invariant",
  "created_at": "2026-11-09T15:26:26Z",
